.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt FILEES-CLIENT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-client
.Nd run one FileES client operation without a background daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm version
.Nm
.Cm autoconfig
.Op Fl -profile Ar path | Fl -activation Ar directory
.Op Fl -state-root Ar directory
.Op Fl -server Ar name
.Op Fl -repo Ar name
.Op Fl -source Ar directory
.Op Fl -name Ar name
.Op Fl -config-root Ar directory
.Op Fl -svn Ar path
.Op Fl -svnmucc Ar path
.Op Fl -ssh Ar path
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Nm
.Cm publish Ar name
.Op Fl -config-root Ar directory
.Op Fl -message Ar text
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Nm
.Cm install | update
.Op Fl -prefix Ar directory
.Op Fl -check
.Op Fl -svn Ar path
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Nm
.Cm activate-begin
.Fl -server-id Ar id
.Fl -server Ar address
.Fl -known-hosts Ar path
.Fl -state-root Ar path
.Fl -email Ar address
.Nm
.Cm activate-finish | activate-resume
.Fl -server-id Ar id
.Fl -server Ar address
.Fl -known-hosts Ar path
.Fl -state-root Ar path
.Op Fl -remote-port Ar port
.Nm
.Cm checkout
.Fl -config Ar path
.Fl -wc Ar id
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Nm
.Cm sync
.Fl -config Ar path
.Fl -wc Ar id
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Op Fl -message Ar text
.Op Fl -nwc
.Op Fl -restore-set | Fl -reverse-reconcile-set
.Nm
.Cm dump-load
.Fl -profile Ar path
.Fl -dump Ar path
.Fl -name Ar name
.Fl -target Ar path
.Fl -state Ar path
.Op Fl -svn Ar path
.Op Fl -ssh Ar path
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Nm
.Cm whale-put | whale-get-quote | whale-get-confirm | whale-status | whale-retry | whale-resume
.Fl -profile Ar path
.Fl -state Ar path
.Op Fl -id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -repo Ar uuid
.Op Fl -path Ar repository-path
.Op Fl -source Ar path
.Op Fl -dest Ar path
.Op Fl -revision Ar number
.Op Fl -timeout Ar duration
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a one-shot FileES client for Linux and
.Ox .
It exits after one operation and may be called by a user's cron job.
It uses an activated FileES identity and a pinned SSH host key.
It is distributed separately from the desktop daemon and the server bundle.
.Cm version
prints the standalone client version and the source revision.
.Pp
.Cm install
and
.Cm update
verify and install the latest signed standalone CLI release.
They require a distribution build containing the trusted release key and
a system Subversion client.
Before executing the initial distribution, verify its manifest signature
with the publisher's trusted public key and check the archive size and SHA-256.
The dedicated CLI channel cannot install desktop or server bundles.
.Fl -prefix
defaults to
.Pa /usr/local
and must be an absolute directory without symbolic links.
Use the same prefix for every subsequent update.
.Fl -check
verifies metadata without downloading the archive or replacing files;
it still creates private update state and requires write access to the prefix.
.Fl -svn
selects the Subversion executable, otherwise found in PATH.
The default installation timeout is 30 minutes.
.Pp
Installation checks signatures, platform binding, expiry, archive size and
SHA-256, and exactly the binary, README and manual.
Each file is replaced atomically, with the executable replaced last.
An interruption may leave newer documentation beside the old program;
repeat the command to finish.
The durable rollback watermark is saved before replacement and permits
retrying the same release while refusing older releases.
The installer's compiled source revision also sets a minimum on first install.
The updater preserves one previous executable and one verified archive.
It does not alter activation, configuration, working copies or cron,
and does not stop a running sync operation.
.Pp
.Cm autoconfig
uses an existing activated profile or an older CLI activation directory,
without another OTP or copying identity keys.
With no repository name it lists the live server repositories.
Select an exact, unambiguous repository display name and an explicit absolute
source directory; the source is canonicalized and never widened to its parent.
Only active, writable ordinary repositories without mandatory edit locks
qualify.
The default activation root is XDG_DATA_HOME/filees/servers or
~/.local/share/filees/servers; use --state-root or --server to select another.
Private jobs are stored below XDG_CONFIG_HOME/filees-cli or
~/.config/filees-cli.
Both commands accept --config-root outside the source.
An existing root must already be private.
Tool paths are discovered once and stored as absolute paths for cron.
Repeating the same configuration is idempotent;
another binding needs another name.
.Pp
.Cm publish Ar name
refreshes the server projection and checks saved client, realm and repository
identities, URL, permissions and monotonic generation before publishing.
Offline or revoked access refuses publication.
It uses the no-working-copy publisher, preserving remotely deleted paths
and never propagating local deletions.
It does not accept restoration or reverse-reconcile flags.
Progress on stderr reports stages and counts without file names.
All changed files are committed atomically; the process automatically sets
the inherited descriptor soft limit for svnmucc, requiring changes plus 64
spare descriptors within the hard limit.
An insufficient hard limit refuses before commit; publication is never split.
The timeout defaults to 30 minutes including permission refresh;
an uncertain commit reply permits an additional 30-second confirmation.
No command installs cron.
.Pp
.Cm activate-finish
and
.Cm activate-resume
use the reverse port saved by onboarding.
An old passport without a saved port requires explicit --remote-port.
.Pp
.Cm checkout
creates a working copy at the path selected by
.Fl -wc .
Without
.Fl -nwc ,
.Cm sync
requires that working copy.
It updates, adds new files, propagates local deletions, and commits changes.
Conflicts stop the operation for manual resolution.
.Pp
.Cm sync Fl -nwc
uses a plain directory and commits new or changed files through
.Xr svnmucc 1 .
The long alias is
.Fl -no-working-copy .
It never propagates local deletions.
By default it does not restore paths deleted from the repository;
.Fl -restore-set
explicitly enables restoration of source-present paths.
.Fl -reverse-reconcile-set
instead downloads one repository revision into the plain directory,
overwrites changed files and removes local paths absent from the accessible
repository view, without committing.
The two set flags are mutually exclusive and require
.Fl -nwc .
No form of
.Fl -nwc
creates a
.Pa .svn
directory.
These are client behaviours, not server-enforced permissions:
the activation retains its ordinary grants.
.Pp
.Cm dump-load
imports one Subversion dump into a newly created repository and a new working
copy.
Both
.Fl -target
and the private
.Fl -state
directory must be dedicated to this import.
On an uncertain result, repeat exactly the same command with the same
.Fl -state ;
the stored operation ID prevents creating another repository.
The existing repository and working copy are never overwritten.
The activation needs permission to create repositories.
.Pp
.Cm whale-put
publishes a source file through FileES Whale.
.Cm whale-get-quote
returns an operation ID and size without downloading.
After reviewing the quote,
.Cm whale-get-confirm
with that ID starts the download to a new destination.
.Cm whale-status ,
.Cm whale-retry ,
and
.Cm whale-resume
read or continue operations in the same private state directory.
No Whale command starts a daemon.
The quote reports size and operation ID; downloading requires a separate
explicit confirmation.
.Pp
A successful confirmed download includes verification of the destination
and confirmation that the server released its download cache and reservation.
The destination may already exist while the operation is still verifying
or has failed to receive that confirmation.
Inspect it with
.Cm whale-status
and use
.Cm whale-retry
after a failure, or
.Cm whale-resume
after a process interruption.
The same operation checks the existing file and retries release without
downloading it again.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The INI file named by
.Fl -config
contains
.Sq tools
(absolute paths for
.Sy svn , svnmucc , ssh
and
.Sy log_dir ) ,
.Sq realm
(identity, known_hosts, host, port and optional
.Sy only ) ,
and one or more
.Sq wc "id"
sections (path and repository-root URL).
The optional
.Sy only
value is an explicit allow-list such as
.Dq !invoices !archive .
The journal directory must exist and be outside a
.Fl -nwc
source.
The CLI never takes an arbitrary source directory or repository URL from a
.Cm sync
command line.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/filees/filees-client.conf
Example invocation profile; the actual path is supplied by
.Fl -config .
.It Pa /var/log/filees-client
Default private journal directory; create it before running the client.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/filees-client-update
Private update state (mode 0700), lock, verified archive cache and
.Pa previous-filees-client .
Below a custom prefix, the same relative path is used.
Do not remove this state to bypass rollback protection.
.It Pa /usr/local/man/man1/filees-client.1
Installed manual on OpenBSD; Linux uses
.Pa /usr/local/share/man/man1/filees-client.1 .
.It Pa state/job.json
Durable
.Cm dump-load
identity, stored below the chosen
.Fl -state
directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors return 2.
Transport, repository, journal and interrupted-operation errors return 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
doas ./bin/filees-client install
doas /usr/local/bin/filees-client update --check
sudo /usr/local/bin/filees-client update
filees-client sync --config /etc/filees/filees-client.conf --wc invoices -nwc
filees-client sync --config /etc/filees/filees-client.conf --wc invoices -nwc -restore-set
filees-client sync --config /etc/filees/filees-client.conf --wc invoices -nwc -reverse-reconcile-set
filees-client dump-load --profile /home/user/.filees/client-profile.json \\
  --dump /home/user/archive.dump --name Invoices-Archive \\
  --target /home/user/archive-wc --state /home/user/.filees/import-001
.Ed
.Pp
After a producer has completed successfully, cron may call the client with
.Cm &&
so a failed producer cannot publish a partial output.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr svn 1 ,
.Xr svnmucc 1 ,
.Xr crontab 5
.Sh CAVEATS
The repository path in a
.Fl -nwc
profile must be its root.
Symbolic links and non-regular source files are refused.
Reverse reconciliation stages downloaded files before changing the local
directory, but application of the complete tree is not atomic; rerun it after
an interruption.
Keep activation keys, profiles and operation state outside published folders.
